    "content": "At a foundation stone-laying ceremony in Puntland, Islaan Bashiir, a respected traditional elder, delivered a speech in which he appealed to Puntland President Said Deni to undertake the construction of a road connecting Garacad and Tuur-dibi. The event, held in the Garacad area, brought together local officials and community members.\n\nThe call comes amid ongoing infrastructure development efforts in Puntland, where improved road networks are seen as crucial for economic growth and connectivity. Garacad, a coastal town in the Mudug region, has been the focus of port development projects in recent years. The proposed road would enhance transportation links between the port and inland areas, facilitating trade and movement.\n\nIslaan Bashiir is among the traditional leaders in Puntland who often use public platforms to highlight community needs and advocate for development projects. His request underscores the importance of infrastructure in fostering regional integration and access to basic services.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, particularly those with ties to Puntland, the construction of such roads is significant. It could improve access to the Garacad port, which is expected to boost trade and create economic opportunities. Diaspora communities often invest in their home regions and rely on efficient infrastructure to support business and family connections.\n\nThe appeal also reflects broader aspirations for stability and development in the region. While no official response from President Deni has been reported, the public request highlights the role of traditional leaders in shaping development priorities.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/islaan-bashiir-oo-madaxweyne-deni-ka-dalbaday-dhismaha-laamiga-garacad-ilaa-tuur-dibi/428031/",
